# Cloudflare Pages: hand every unmatched path to the Angular router.
#
# Without this, only "/" exists as a real file. Loading /search?q=lighthouse
# directly, refreshing on /item/123, or following a shared link would all 404,
# because Pages looks for a file at that path and there isn't one.
#
# The 200 (rather than a 301/302) matters: the URL stays as the user typed it,
# so the router still sees /item/123 and renders the right page.
/*    /index.html   200
